"A1 iteration 4 is done. The final engine is `e3-1.5.0` and its change record is written. With all 27 A1 cases running, G2(b)\u2013(e) now pass. G2(a), G2(f) and G3 still fail.\n\n**What happened first.** This was the third start of iteration 4. The second start had edited the engine (fixes 1\u20138) and hit its session limit before writing a record. I kept the original 09:33 snapshot instead of re-taking it, because a new one would have captured that half-edited engine; the snapshot equals iteration 3's final engine. Then I reviewed and validated those eight fixes and kept them. The G3 truth table had frozen after iteration 3's measure step, so all 27 A1 cases ran through the engine, 13 of them for the first time.\n\n**Fixes I added** (all geometric; no SKU, family or filename logic; nothing in `eval/` or `compile/` changed):\n- **Fix 9, joggle risers.** On the real 10839000 scans the joggle riser is a smooth S with no flat part, so a line search can lock onto any angle. The riser angle now comes from the measured step to the far flange. The two riser flange lengths become UNKNOWN(UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE), and joggle angles carry a large uncertainty, so they read REVIEW. This is a stated convention, not a plane fit.\n- **Fix 10, near-symmetric parts.** The two 180\u00b0 images of the part are now told apart by their holes. On all three 10839000 scans this confirms the engine's existing choice by a wide margin.\n- **Fix 11, bowed panels.** Near each bend, a panel's plane is re-fitted on its own material. The 460 mm datum of 23553000 is bowed 1\u20132 mm at its ends, which had left 5 bends unmeasured.\n- **Fix 12, window holes.** The second start's tighter hole clearance (fix 4) now applies only to round holes. It had broken two 38172000 test probes; the probes it was made for still read correctly.\n\n**Results, before \u2192 after** (all 27 cases, best-F1 lane on the same scans in brackets):\n\n| Measure | Before (fixes 1\u20138) | Final |\n|---|---|---|\n| G2(c) known-good angle error | 3.49\u00b0 FAIL | 0.795\u00b0 PASS |\n| G2(d) known-good flange P95 | 16.0 mm FAIL | 0.392 mm PASS |\n| G2(b) coverage, angle / flange | 79/85, 150/166 | 84/85, 160/166 |\n| G3 state match | 0.927 | 0.959 |\n| GOLD_SET_V1 line-F1 (micro / family-macro) | 0.924 / 0.942 | 0.977 / 0.966 (0.566 / 0.583) |\n| Gold11 relabel line-F1 | 0.919 | 0.987, P 0.975, R 1.000 (0.547) |\n| BROAD family-macro line-F1 | 0.801 | 0.806 (0.543) |\n| Per-bend correctness given CAD (riser lengths allowed / strict) | 0.798 / 0.788 | 0.872 / 0.818 |\n| False-PASS proxy | 3 | 3 |\n\nOf the 3 false-PASS proxies, 2 are the disputed 10839000 scan_2 rows below and 1 is a 38172000 SCAN_1 line no gold confirms; none changed. The synthetic regression tier passes with every accuracy number identical to before. 131 focused tests pass. Every heavy job ran under the shared lock.\n\n**Still failing:**\n- **G2(a):** fails on the human Gold11 set, which the frozen scorer still uses as gate of record (F1 0.391). It passes on the relabel.\n- **G2(f):** repeatability is 0.426\u00b0. The three 15651004 \"repeats\" are actually three different stages.\n- **G3, 4 rows on 10839000 scan_2 (B6, B8, B9, B11):** I think the frozen truth table is wrong here. Under the engine's pose, both short walls' holes and the 30\u00d718 mm cut-out line up exactly with the scan. Under the 180\u00b0 pose that matches the table, the holes land 7\u20139 mm off and the cut-out sits on solid sheet. Renders are in `diag/`. I did not change the engine to match the table; these rows need re-adjudication through the G3 procedure.\n- **G3, other items:** 28870000 SCAN_1 (a rolled part, still flagged as possibly the wrong part), and a known-good angle error of 1.19\u00b0. That figure is driven by 10839000's 90\u00b0 bends reading 1\u20132\u00b0 overbent on every scan, which the legacy arm also sees, so it looks real.\n\n**Open risks:**\n- On 23553000 FULL, fix 12 moved the datum pose 0.65 mm to a slightly better-scoring one. The short hook flanges B5\u2013B7 then shifted about 1.2 mm, going from PASS to FAIL against an uncertainty of 0.1\u20130.15 mm. One of the two readings must be wrong, so this scan may hold a false PASS or a false FAIL. It is not a known-good part, so no gate sees it. This is the first thing to fix next iteration.\n- Fix 11 turned some 23553000 bow-end bends into position FAILs (\u22121.50 and \u22122.99 mm). The bow is real, but whether it is a defect or from the fixture is unknown.\n- I did not re-run the full sweep of 84 synthetic probes on the final engine, only the regressed and targeted ones.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/a1/iter_4/`:\n- CHANGE.md\n- engine.diff\n- engine_before.tgz\n- validation/\n- diag/\n- tools/\n\nThe engine edits are in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/domains/production/engine/inspect/` (articulated.py, config.py, engine.py, metrology.py, registration.py). The new tests are in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/tests/test_prod_engine_inspect_a1_iter4.py`."